# Noise-Stable Prime Spectrum in Definable Quantum Walks

## Overview

This file lays the *spectral* foundation for the conjecture that the eigenphase
distribution of arithmetic quantum walks on Cayley graphs `Cay(ZMod n, S)`
exhibits an arithmetic noise-stability/instability dichotomy governed by the
prime factorization of `n`.

The carrier of every discrete-time quantum walk on an abelian Cayley graph is the
*circulant* (group-algebra) operator whose eigenvalues are the additive-character
sums

  `λ_S(j) = ∑_{s ∈ S} ψ(j · s)`,  with `ψ = ZMod.stdAddChar` the standard
  additive character `x ↦ exp(2πi x / n)`.

These character sums *are* the eigenvalues of the walk generator simultaneously
diagonalized in the Fourier basis, so understanding them is exactly understanding
the spectral measure. We establish four structural pillars:

* `ceig_zero_eq_card`     — the trivial (Perron) eigenvalue equals the degree `|S|`.
* `ceig_total`            — spectral trace / orthogonality: `∑_j λ_S(j) = n·[0∈S]`.
* `ceig_conj`             — symmetric step sets give a *real* (Hermitian) spectrum.
* `ceig_complete`         — the complete Cayley graph has spectrum `{ |n|-1, -1 }`,
                             the extremal maximally-degenerate (fragile) walk.
* `weig_perturbation_le`  — eigenvalues are `1`-Lipschitz in the `ℓ¹` gate weight,
                             i.e. a noise-stability (Wasserstein-`O(ε)`) bound,
  with corollary `weig_perturbation_uniform` giving the explicit `|T|·ε` bound.

## Catalog synthesis

This module is the spectral-number-theory companion to the catalog's expander
and character-sum machinery (`Algebra/ClassicalGroupExpanders`,
`Algebra/ExpanderWalk/Amplification`): there one studies the *spectral gap* of
random walks; here we expose the *full eigenphase law* of the unitary walk and
its stability under gate noise. The complete-graph computation `ceig_complete`
is the abelian Cayley analogue of the complete-graph spectrum used implicitly in
expander amplification.

